  "notes": "Derived from the revised AI-generated sheet, matching the supplied reference with requested edits. Automatically reduced grid interpretation; small details differ from the reference. Grip/pivot/muzzle are initial estimates requiring rig checks. Preview slot W05 confirmed from repository pixelkit-v2 manifest at ae7247a9b94aeb834342cd40e8aea2eb82308bb8. This does not add firing behaviours.\nRevision: weapons-v001. Status: draft. Pixel cleanup and anchor/scale review outstanding. Stored in isolated art/weapon-lab branch.\n\nLaser-sequence-v001: four two-pixel red barrel lamps at x=26/29/32/35, y=9. Smooth overlapping rear-to-muzzle sequence; 32 frames at 20 fps (1.6 s). Eight body pixels form dark red unlit lamp seats; silhouette, alpha, anchors, trim, guts and scale unchanged. Existing cyan emissive remains a smooth pulse. Ambient loop only, no firing timing. Draft; gameplay-size recognition approval pending.\n\nAnchor-alignment-v001: calibrated handle grip and muzzle for the enlarged weapon rig. Body and all animation layers unchanged. Runtime scales around the grip; ranged shots use the transformed muzzle. Scale remains 1.2. Pending alignment verification.\n\nArt Pass V2: material-family harmonisation. Eight-step neutral charcoal/gunmetal ramp derived from the generated V2 material reference. Original pixel geometry, alpha, markers, scale, dimensions, fps, frame count, emissive PNGs, trim and guts are unchanged. Every frame uses the same RGB material mapping. Existing cyan, magenta, red and amber light identities and all original loops retained. Source is the current shared build 20261101T094357Z-78228871. Saved draft; renderer comparison only; battle playtest and art approval pending.",
